{"step_index":423,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-27T17:22:19Z","content":"I have successfully implemented all the requested changes to prepare the application for cloud deployment:\n\n### 1. Dynamic API URL (`app.js`)\nAt the top of `app.js`, I added the `API_BASE_URL` constant that automatically detects if the frontend is running locally or in production (Vercel). I then replaced all the hardcoded `http://127.0.0.1:8000` strings across the three `fetch()` calls (`/api/tles`, `/api/conjunctions`, and `/api/mission-risk`) to dynamically use `${API_BASE_URL}`.\n\n### 2. Permissive CORS for Vercel (`main.py`)\nChecked the `CORSMiddleware` configuration in `main.py`. The `allow_origins=[\"*\"]` setting was already present and properly configured, so cross-origin requests from the Vercel frontend will not be blocked.\n\n### 3. Production Server Ready (`main.py`)\nModified the `uvicorn.run()` block at the bottom of `main.py` to bind to `host=\"0.0.0.0\"` and read the port from the `PORT` environment variable (defaulting to 8000), making it fully compatible with cloud hosting providers like Render, Heroku, or Fly.io.\n\nEverything is updated and ready for production!"}
